{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: implement the combined thread record-detail repair and carry, as one head on current main. This is a child of 69bd36a7, which I promised as 92eb0af9; I am handing the implementation to you and will close the parent when your work merges. Hugh directed the handoff and directed that all the changes come in together.\n\nWHY ONE HEAD RATHER THAN TWO. Codex requested changes on 43daa5f0 in verdict 8f00fe1f, which I ratified as cc3a7201, and said plainly that any repair needs new exact-head artifacts and review. Separately, 43daa5f0 branches from 7a02f3e1 and is three merges behind main, while 69bd36a7 requires starting from current main. Repairing in place and then carrying would cost two review passes and put the second one on a base that is stale again by the time it lands. So repair, carry and union in one head, reviewed once.\n\nWHAT I ALREADY LEARNED TRYING THE CARRY, so you do not repeat it. I rebased the seven commits of 43daa5f0 onto 7e7b8412. Four apply cleanly. Conflicts in internal/service/uidist are only the generated embed -- resolve by regenerating with make ui, never by hand-merging. RequestList.tsx has a real but easy conflict where main adds a vocabulary binding and the branch lifts sort, query and population into a view prop: keep both. The blocker is commit 75a1eb33 against merged 511335e7, and it is a design collision, not a resolution. Do not resolve it by taking either side: taking the branch side silently deletes ratificationRows and the \"awaiting ratification\" lifecycle state from ui/src/lib/rows.ts, which is merged main behaviour, and I nearly shipped that regression. Recorded in asserts 4729a06a and 56c8f6d4.\n\nTHE UNION Hugh authorised. Main renders three summary links and carries \"awaiting ratification\" plus ratificationRows(projection, vocabulary, context) returning rows and ratifiers. The branch replaces the links with five tabs over a uniform workRows(projection, context, population) for live, moved, stale, done, closed. Deliver six tabs: those five plus awaiting ratification. Ratification takes different inputs and returns a different shape, so the populations map has to accommodate that rather than pretend it is a sixth workRows population.\n\nCODEX'S TWO OUTSTANDING FINDINGS, both of which must be closed in this head.\n\nFirst, explicit expansion is untested. Codex set the show-all button's onClick to undefined in a mutation worktree and all 71 UI tests still passed. Add a DOM interaction test with more than twelve references that clicks the button, observes all thirty in order, and fails when the handler is disabled. Verify by performing that mutation yourself and watching the new test fail; a green suite is not evidence.\n\nSecond, and more serious, the ratification closing station can name a retired ratification as current. buildSpine uses projection.acts.find for the first effective ratify act, but projected acts keep their original effective verdict after retirement. The fold's activeRatification takes the latest surviving effective ratification. So ratify A, supersede A, ratify B renders as closed by A when B is live. Codex's instruction is right and I am passing it on unchanged: do not reproduce authority semantics approximately in the UI. Use one shared selector whose ordering and retirement rule visibly match the fold, or project the current ratification explicitly, and add a regression that distinguishes A from B.","body":{"area":"ui","base":"7e7b8412bcd95e3d3345a481b72febc502513109","branch":"request/thread-record-detail-v2","conditions":"One head on current main 7e7b8412, branch request/thread-record-detail-v2, own worktree. Carry all seven commits of 43daa5f0 forward; regenerate the uidist embed with make ui rather than merging it. Preserve every behaviour the earlier reviews accepted: one native disclosure button with correct aria state, nested reference navigation without accidental toggle, second-click close, unreached plain text, elided act detail, one threadRoot rule, fold decision sequence, list state surviving unmount and return, the single memoized RecordIndex passed from App, get-or-create reverse-provenance buckets, and index reads instead of projection scans. Preserve merged main behaviour: ratificationRows and the awaiting-ratification lifecycle state must survive. Deliver six population tabs: live, moved, stale, done, closed, awaiting ratification. Close codex's two findings from ratified verdict cc3a7201: a DOM interaction test proving explicit expansion of more than twelve references, verified by mutating the handler to undefined and watching it fail; and a shared active-ratification selector matching the fold's latest-surviving-effective rule, with a regression distinguishing ratify A, supersede A, ratify B. Gates: npm test, make ui, make ui-check including tsc and embed parity, go test -race ./..., go vet, git diff --check, clean worktree, pushed. Publish exact-head ui and internal/service artifacts and request independent review from codex with Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions.","parent_request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f3572ad6ea2c8ccfa47687f51f256dfa69bd36a7","reviewer":"codex","source_head":"43daa5f03f3d662b7ab2ce83c63c05d753eb1aeb","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}